This is an implementation of the model of Ghiorso, M. S. & Sack, R. O. 1995,
Contributions to Mineralogy and Petrology, 119, 197. This model stands at the
basis of the MELTS code https://gitlab.com/ENKI-portal/ThermoEngine.git . The
present implementation follows the description by Ghiorso & Sack 1995. But to
ensure that the formulas are correctly implemented, the formulas in the
model_GhiorsoSack1995.py are copies from the equivalent formulas from the
LiquidMelts*.m files of the MELTS code.

The MELTS code itself has some updates and changes compared to the original GS95
model. In particular, several new components were added. They are included in
the liquid model here. The MELTS code also has updated mineral data (compared to
the original Ghiorso & Sack 1995 paper), which are _not_ included in the public
version of PhaseHull, but can be obtained upon request to the author (CPD).

The MELTS code also has numerous solid solutions implemented, which are _not_
included in the PhaseHull implementation yet. They may be implemented in the
future, but then they will not be in the public version of PhaseHull, but may
be obtained upon request to the author (CPD).

Another important difference is the implementation of H2O, which should not
be used (so far) as it is not properly implemented yet.

So please use this implementation of the Ghiorso & Sack model with care, as it
is not guaranteed to properly match the MELTS code. It is, if anything, a
highly simplified "MELTS-lite" implementation.

